<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lahaul</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lahul</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lahaul is a high mountain valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, north of the Rohtang Pass, drained by the Chandra and Bhaga rivers. Its people combine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhist</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> traditions, and it lay on the trade routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kullu">Kullu</a> and Ladakh, whose kings disputed its control. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spiti">Spiti</a> it now forms Lahaul and Spiti district, and the Atal Tunnel, opened in 2020, links it to Kullu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lahaul.jpg" alt="Lahaul" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This Photo was taken by Timothy A. Gonsalves. Feel free to use my photos, but please mention me as the author. … · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kardhang_Biling_Bhaga_Dhauladhar_Oct22_A7C_04645.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
